sym2 -- symmetric square of a chain complex
*******************************************

  * Usage: 
        G = sym2 F
  * Inputs:
      * F, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 
  * Outputs:
      * G, a *note complex: (Complexes)Complex,, 

Description
===========

If tau: F**F \to F**F is the chain map reversing the factors, with appropriate
signs, then sym2 F = image(1+tau) = ker(1-tau) = coker(1-tau)



Ways to use sym2:
=================

  * "sym2(Complex)"

