testWalker -- tests Walker's formula
************************************

  * Usage: 
        t = testWalker M
  * Inputs:
      * M, a *note module: (Macaulay2Doc)Module,, of finite length
  * Outputs:
      * t, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, 

Description
===========

Verifies Walker's Theorem for a finite length graded module over a polynomial
ring of char not 2: (2^(codim M)*length M + sum toList (excess M)) == (sum of
the betti numbers of M)*(length M)

Caveat
======

Returns an error if any homology has infinite length

